  "id": "RLSA-2026:102194",
  "title": "Moderate: curl security update",
  "issued": {
    "date": "2026-11-24 06:01:09"
  },
  "updated": {
    "date": "2026-11-28 00:04:27"
  },
  "severity": "Moderate",
  "description": "The curl packages provide the libcurl library and the curl utility for downloading files from servers using various protocols, including HTTP, FTP, and LDAP.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* curl: curl: Security bypass due to global TLS option changes in multi-threaded LDAPS transfers (CVE-2025-14017)\n\n* curl: libcurl: Use-after-free in HTTP/2 Server Push with shared connections (CVE-2026-18924)\n\n* curl: curl: Public key pinning bypass allows unauthenticated connections (CVE-2026-80230)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
